id: pm-iop1pg
title: "GH-1516: queued writers fail at a fixed lock deadline even while the lock is changing hands"
description: "locks.wait_ms (default 3000) is a total wall-clock budget, so with ~20 concurrent writers on one plain-directory tracker most writers exhaust it while the lock is handed from writer to writer and fail with lock_conflict (exit 4); their comments/creates are lost unless each agent retries. A live, progressing queue is indistinguishable from a stuck owner."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: bug,concurrency,locks,multi-agent,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-22T18:10:30.531Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T00:10:16.126Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-22T19:15:15.063Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T19:15:15.063Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "For lock acquisitions using the progress wait policy (the item-store mutation lease, restore and the hierarchy-integrity lock), a waiter fails only when the SAME lock owner holds the lock for the configured wait window without progress, or a hard ceiling is reached; Every observed owner handoff (token change or release) restarts the no-progress window for those acquisitions; The default total wait policy of acquireLock/acquireLockLease, explicit maxWaitMs ceilings (background consumers) and wait 0 fail-fast are unchanged; The conflict receipt reports waited time and observed owner handoffs; A multi-process conformance test runs many concurrent writers (comments + parented creates) on one non-git tracker and loses zero writes under a short wait window; Docs for locks.wait_ms and PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS describe which locks use the no-progress semantics"
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
repro_steps: "See GH-1516: 20 background shells each running pm create --parent, pm comments --add, pm update on one plain-directory tracker."
resolution: "Queued writers behind a progressing lock on the GH-1516 contention paths (item-store mutations, restore, parented creates and other hierarchy-integrity mutations) now commit instead of failing at a fixed 3 s deadline; a stalled single owner still refuses after the budget. The policy is opt-in (waitPolicy progress) so short internal locks (foreground telemetry, usage ledger, derived index) and public acquireLock callers keep their exact budgets, and PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS can still raise them. Multi-process conformance (10 comments + 10 parented creates, PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS=1000) loses zero writes and fails on the previous build. Per-parent hierarchy lock scope and lock-free appends remain on pm-lvyd."
expected_result: Concurrent writers queued behind a progressing lock all commit; only a stalled owner or the hard ceiling produces lock_conflict.
actual_result: All 20 concurrent writers committed in the conformance test; stalled-owner and maxWaitMs-ceiling controls refuse as specified.
dependencies[2]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-gh1549,related,"2026-10-22T18:10:30.531Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
  pm-lvyd,implements,"2026-10-22T18:10:30.531Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T21:16:40.841Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (PR #1550): the handoff-restarted window is now OPT-IN via acquireLock/acquireLockLease options { waitPolicy: 'progress' }. Default stays a fixed total budget so short-budget internal locks (foreground telemetry 250 ms, context usage ledger, derived-index lock) and public acquireLock callers keep their exact latency contract, and PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS can still raise them (capping them with maxWaitMs would have removed that escape hatch). Enabled on the item-store lease, restore and the hierarchy-integrity lock, which are the GH-1516 contention paths."
